# Erdős Problem #99 — LA90 propagation through the Type-II global ledgers

**Date:** 2026-09-14  
**Target:** Target C-II, canonical full-core Type-II branch  
**Repository base:** `c710dd5e` on `research/c2-gluing-sol-20260914-r9`  
**Claim class:** proof-only propagation of LA90 (`eta_grid=0.0009`)  
**External input:** none beyond the already-audited Section-171 and stopped-train stack  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN`

LA90 raises the proof-only atomic train gain to

\[
\eta_{grid}=g=0.0009.
\]

Its source note deliberately stopped before recomputing the Section-171 endpoint and the downstream chamber/rhombus/residual constants. This note performs that propagation. No new local geometry is asserted here.

Put

\[
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3},\qquad
s_2=\sqrt{\Delta_2},\qquad
\rho=0.7390851332151606\ldots,
\]

where `rho=cos(rho)`, and

\[
C_{146}={4\over9}(\pi+s_2)
=1.8195135379794447\ldots .
\]

## 1. Correlated stopped-train split

The exact identity

\[
\rho_{rec}+\sigma_R-q
=2\left(T-{q\over2}-2\sqrt{R_4}\right)
\]

and LA90 give

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\rho_{rec}+\sigma_R-q\over D}\ge0.0018.
}
\tag{L90.1}
\]

Using `q/D>=2rho-o(1)`,

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\rho_{rec}+\sigma_R\over D}
\ge2\rho+0.0018
=1.479970266430321\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.2}
\]

Therefore at least one of

\[
\boxed{
S={\rho_{rec}\over2}
\ge\left({\rho\over2}+0.00045-o(1)\right)D
=0.369992566607580\ldots D-o(D)
}
\tag{L90.3}
\]

or

\[
\boxed{
\sigma_R\ge(\rho+0.0009-o(1))D
=0.739985133215161\ldots D-o(D)
}
\tag{L90.4}
\]

must hold.

On the rhombic branch,

\[
M_R={\sigma_R\over8}
\left(4\sqrt{R_4}+{\sigma_R\over2}\right)
\]

gives

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {M_R\over D^2}
\ge {\rho+0.0009\over8}
\left(4s_2+{\rho+0.0009\over2}\right)
=0.386572284461081\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.5}
\]

The exact post-endpoint scalar identity also improves by `(0.0009-0.00058)/5` relative to P58:

\[
\boxed{
\liminf\mu_D\ge1.785559210824532\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.6}
\]

The direct correlated endpoint/interface floor becomes

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {J\over D}
\ge2\rho+4s_2-\pi+0.0018
=2.147628840296357\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.7}
\]

## 2. Section-171 endpoint with `g=0.0009`

Audited Section 171 reduces every Type-II subsequential limit

\[
t=\lim{q-k\over D},\qquad
\delta=\lim{b-P_F\over D}\ge0
\]

to

\[
F_t(\delta)=
10t-5\pi-5\delta
+\left(81(\pi+\delta)^2\delta\right)^{1/3}
-{8\Delta_2\over9t/2-2\pi-2\delta}
\ge0.
\tag{L90.8}
\]

With train gain `g`, the feasible detour interval is

\[
0\le\delta\le
{{9\over2}(t-C_{146})-g\over2}.
\tag{L90.9}
\]

Take

\[
g=0.0009,\qquad
\varepsilon_{90}=0.0014758,
\qquad
t_{90}=C_{146}+\varepsilon_{90}.
\tag{L90.10}
\]

Then

\[
\boxed{
t_{90}=1.8209893379794447\ldots
}
\tag{L90.11}
\]

and the right endpoint of the feasible detour interval is exactly

\[
\boxed{
\delta_{90}=0.00287055.
}
\tag{L90.12}
\]

At this endpoint the denominator in the last term of (L90.8) simplifies exactly to

\[
2s_2+g.
\]

The exact-rational certificate `verify_target_c_la90_global_propagation.py` proves:

1. `F_{t90}` is strictly increasing on `0<=delta<=delta90`;
2. `F_{t90}(delta90)<0`, with outward-rounding margin greater than `4e-5`;
3. `partial F_t(delta)/partial t>0` throughout the feasible domain.

Hence every feasible `delta` gives `F_{t90}(delta)<0`. For `t<t90`, the admissible detour interval only shrinks and `F_t(delta)<F_{t90}(delta)` at fixed `delta`. Thus no Type-II limit can satisfy `t<=t90`.

Therefore

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {q-k\over D}
\ge C_{146}+0.0014758
=1.8209893379794447\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.13}
\]

A direct high-precision numerical solve of the same endpoint equation gives

\[
\varepsilon_*=0.0014759617517679997\ldots,
\]

so the certified value retains about `1.62e-7` of offset slack. Further decimal tuning of this scalar endpoint is not a useful closure route.

## 3. Mandatory chamber/interface floor

Using

\[
{T-q/2\over D}\ge2s_2+0.0009-o(1),
\]

`J=2T-P_F`, `P_F/D->pi`, and (L90.13),

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {J\over D}
\ge j_{90}:=t_{90}+2(2s_2+0.0009)-\pi
=2.490447911845481\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.14}
\]

The chamber decomposition

\[
\Sigma_{ch}=J+a+L_{add}+R_F
\]

therefore gives

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\Sigma_{ch}\over D}
\ge2.490447911845481\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.15}
\]

As in P58, this is mandatory interface complexity, not free packing spare.

## 4. `H` bootstrap and linear rhombus deficit

The exact relation

\[
H={J\over2}+(q-k)-{P_F\over2}
\]

gives

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {H\over D}
\ge h_{90}:={j_{90}\over2}+t_{90}-{\pi\over2}
=1.495416967107289\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.16}
\]

Hence

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {A_{ch}-a_0Z_{ch}\over D}
\ge {\sqrt3\over4}h_{90}
=0.647534541382595\ldots,
}
\tag{L90.17}
\]

and

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {\Delta_2D^2-R_4\over D}
\ge {h_{90}\over2}
=0.747708483553644\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.18}
\]

## 5. Corrected residual budget

The finite corrected residual cap remains

\[
R_F+\Sigma_{ext}
<{P_K\over2}+P_F-q-{\delta_K+E_4\over a_0}.
\]

Using `q>=q-k`, `P_K,P_F<=pi D`, and (L90.13),

\[
\boxed{
\limsup {R_F+\Sigma_{ext}\over D}
\le {3\pi\over2}-t_{90}
=2.891399642405245\ldots .
}
\tag{L90.19}
\]

The stronger atomic theorem therefore continues to move the two first-order ledgers in the desired directions: mandatory chamber/interface complexity increases and genuine residual allowance decreases. Their present scalar gap is still far from a contradiction.

## 6. What changed, and what did not

Relative to the earlier `g=0.00058` propagation:

- the certified `(q-k)/D` offset rises from `0.0014085` to `0.0014758`;
- the singleton alternative rises to `0.3699925666D-o(D)`;
- the rhombic alternative rises to `0.7399851332D-o(D)` and `M_R>=0.3865722844D^2-o(D^2)`;
- the mandatory chamber floor rises to `2.4904479118D-o(D)`;
- the corrected residual cap falls to `2.8913996424D+o(D)`.

None of these scalar improvements closes C-II. LA90 itself identifies the next possible atomic improvement as a direct six-cross-label optimization, but the one-pair architecture is already near its numerical ceiling. The more promising closure work is therefore structural: combine the stronger low-`t` endpoint with the newly proved pentagon/network and outer-tooth/long-side constraints on `main`.

**Disposition:** proof-only LA90 propagation. C-II and Level I remain open.
